            <ArticleTitle>Paravalvular aortic rupture causing angina following aortic valve replacement.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>321-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the first encounter of a paravalvular rupture of the aorta 5 years after aortic valve replacement with a #25 Omniscience tilting disc. The rupture involved the circumflex coronary artery causing angina.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
